src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol:_exitPool|class=C23|High|On any CurveInterface.V2 vault whose Curve crypto pool holds WETH (not ALT_ETH), every exit passes the literal use_eth = true while entry passes the derived 0 < msgValue (== false), so the pool pushes native ETH out; the two-sided path then measures the delta on the WETH ERC20 and records exitBalances[wethLeg] == 0, silently deleting that leg from the redeemer's proceeds and from __initiateWithdraw's request (which skips zero balances), while the single-sided path reports WETH it does not hold and bricks the asset payout — any unprivileged depositor loses the ETH leg on redemption.|src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol
